{"questions":[{"question_id":"1lg1ojzyh","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2007 Paper 1 Offline","year":2007,"examDate":2007,"subject":"physics","chapter":"work-power-and-energy","chapterGroup":"mechanics","topic":"work","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"pstatement-1p-pa-block-of-mass-m-starts-moving-on-a-r-jee-advanced-physics-motion-y9gfnvvg6rdrzr6q","content":"<p><b>Statement 1 :</b></p>\n<p>A block of mass m starts moving on a rough horizontal surface with a velocity v. It stops due to friction between the block and the surface after moving through a certain distance. The surface is now tilted to an angle of 30<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.988ex\" height=\"1.532ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -677 436.6 677\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(33,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2218\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2218\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> with the horizontal and the same block is made to go up on the surface with the same initial velocity v. The decrease in the mechanical energy in the second situation is smaller than that in the first situation.</p>\n<p><b>Statement 2 :</b></p>\n<p>The coefficient of friction between the block and the surface decreases with the increase in the angle of inclination.</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Statement 1 is True, Statement 2 is True, Statement 2 is a CORRECT explanation for Statement 1"},{"identifier":"B","content":"Statement 1 is True, Statement 2 is True, Statement 2 is NOT a CORRECT explanation for Statement 1"},{"identifier":"C","content":"Statement 1 is True, Statement 2 is False"},{"identifier":"D","content":"Statement 1 is False, Statement 2 is True"}],"correct_options":["C"],"explanation":"<p>Case I:</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1mggcyk9w/6512382d-c473-4c73-b612-87fce076895c/16c62e40-a360-11f0-b814-0f72f73fa4cf/file-jaoe38c1mggcyk9x.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/jaoe38c1mggcyk9w/6512382d-c473-4c73-b612-87fce076895c/16c62e40-a360-11f0-b814-0f72f73fa4cf/file-jaoe38c1mggcyk9x.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto;max-height:40vh;vertical-align:baseline\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2007 Paper 1 Offline Physics - Work Power &amp; Energy Question 4 English Explanation\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/jaoe38c1mggcyk9w/6512382d-c473-4c73-b612-87fce076895c/16c62e40-a360-11f0-b814-0f72f73fa4cf/file-jaoe38c1mggcyk9x.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/jaoe38c1mggcyk9w/6512382d-c473-4c73-b612-87fce076895c/16c62e40-a360-11f0-b814-0f72f73fa4cf/file-jaoe38c1mggcyk9x.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1mggcyk9w/6512382d-c473-4c73-b612-87fce076895c/16c62e40-a360-11f0-b814-0f72f73fa4cf/file-jaoe38c1mggcyk9x.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/jaoe38c1mggcyk9w/6512382d-c473-4c73-b612-87fce076895c/16c62e40-a360-11f0-b814-0f72f73fa4cf/file-jaoe38c1mggcyk9x.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/jaoe38c1mggcyk9w/6512382d-c473-4c73-b612-87fce076895c/16c62e40-a360-11f0-b814-0f72f73fa4cf/file-jaoe38c1mggcyk9x.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/jaoe38c1mggcyk9w/6512382d-c473-4c73-b612-87fce076895c/16c62e40-a360-11f0-b814-0f72f73fa4cf/file-jaoe38c1mggcyk9x.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>Case II : Tilted at 30<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 